facts:
A vector is written with an undertilde, as $\underset{\sim}{a}$, or from start point to end point, as $\overrightarrow{AB}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4,2.2);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[->,thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway,above left] {$\underset{\sim}{a}=\overrightarrow{AB}$};
\node[below] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

